6cfe7d` |\n| N60_LIVE_PRODUCT_PROOF | NOT_AVAILABLE | `4d9e8ff47a0dc966e2fa54f71550be4ac66ed5f76f04229cabe0891ca7da2fd9` |\n\n`requirements/plan26.lock` sha256 `df971a783b9d027db96eae800e33e7bc65471b94f7a3b0a151eec075e0824835` — unchanged since N10, byte-identical across every citing node.\n\n### Finding F1 — evidence drift (RESOLVED by N90; non-blocking)\n\n**rework_edges key:** `evidence_integrity_drift` · **owning node:** `N40_CLI_CUTOVER`\n\nFirst-pass hash recomputation found `results/evidence/N40_CLI_CUTOVER` did not\nmatch its receipt. Root cause: two evidence files\n(`plan25_resume_refusal.txt`, `preflight_read_only.txt`) had uncommitted local\nedits containing a different tmp path and, notably, `engine_root`/\n`curriculum_root` pointing at the live repo rather than an isolated attempt\nsandbox — the signature of directly re-invoking N40's CLI verification\ncommands outside harness sandboxing. This traces to the immediately prior\n`N90_FINAL_AUDIT` attempt (`attempt-20260813T000636...`), whose own log shows\na user interrupt mid-session (`\"[Request interrupted by user]\"`) and whose\nfinal scheduler event is `\"status\":\"BLOCKED\",\"reason\":\"claude_failed\"` — it\nnever reached a written verdict and left stray uncommitted edits.\n\nThis was **not** a code or spec change: `git status --porcelain` confirmed\nonly those two evidence files were dirty, nothing under `runtime/` or\n`plans/.../spec` or `plans/.../implementation.graph.v3.yaml`. N90 restored\nboth files to their last-committed state via `git checkout --`. Second-pass\nrecomputation: **0 mismatches across all 15 receipts.** Full detail:\n`evidence/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/receipt_hash_verification.txt`.\n\n### Finding F2 — receipt provenance staleness (CLOSED by direct re-verification; non-blocking)\n\n**rework_edges key:** `receipt_cascade_invalidation` · **owning node:** harness/`prompt_graph_controller.py` (not a curriculum N-node — a scheduler bookkeeping gap)\n\n`N40_CLI_CUTOVER` (receipt `created_at` 2026-08-12T18:09:11Z),\n`N50_ADVERSARIAL_REGRESSION` (18:31:55Z), and `N60_LIVE_PRODUCT_PROOF`\n(18:47:45Z) all predate a later rework cycle — patches `P-N20-002`,\n`P-N31-001..003`, `P-N32-001..002` — whose receipts (`N32` 23:59:06Z, `N20`\n00:05:00Z, `N30` 00:05:50Z, `N31` 00:06:03Z, all 2026-08-12/13) postdate them\nby 5-6 hours. `git show --stat` on the intervening commit `165555d` confirms\nit modified `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py` (+102 lines),\n`acceptance.py` (+163), and `repair.py` (+96) — files N50's adversarial suite\ndirectly exercises. The manifest's own rule\n(`rules.invalidate_descendants_on_rework: true`) implies N50/N60 should have\nbeen invalidated and re-run after this, but their receipts were never\nrefreshed. Full timeline: `evidence/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/receipt_provenance_timeline.txt`.\n\nThis is **not** a functional defect — it is closed, not merely noted, because\nN90 independently reran the complete regression suite against the current,\nfinal, post-rework code (not the stale receipt) and it passed clean (section\n5). The P-N20-002/P-N32-002 patch bodies were also read directly: both are\nscoped test-assertion corrections (upgrading a placeholder \"must not reach a\nreal terminal yet\" assertion into a genuine positive `UNIT_ACCEPTED` check,\nnow that D24-D32 wiring is complete), explicitly forbidding any other file\ntouch, and neither weakens or removes a test. **Recommendation (non-blocking,\nprocess hygiene):** the controller should auto-invalidate descendant receipts\nwhen an ancestor node is reworked post-hoc, per its own stated rule.\n\n## 3. Exactly one compiled LangGraph production path (TEST item 3)\n\n- Single `StateGraph(...)`/`.compile(...)` pair: `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py:601,612`.\n- Single definition of `build_curriculum_factory_graph` (`graph.py:575`); exactly two call sites, both in `runtime/run_curriculum.py` (fresh-episode and resume-episode branches of the one live path), both invoking the same function.\n- No `import`/`from` of `langchain` (top-level package; `langchain_core`, LangGraph's own dependency, is excluded from the check per `implementation.graph.v3.yaml`'s `forbidden_production_imports` list), `langchain_openai`, `langchain_google_genai`, `openai`, or `google.generativeai` anywhere under `runtime/`.\n- No `session_bridge`, `CROSS_FAMILY_BYPASS`, `ACCEPTED_PENDING_REVIEW`, `--test-simulated*`, or `controller.simulate` reachable from production (`runtime/langgraph_factory/*.py`, `runtime/run_curriculum.py`).\n- CLI `--help` (rerun live, current code) exposes exactly `--preflight | --unit | --all | --resume`, each requiring `--authorization` except read-only `--preflight` — no legacy path.\n\nFull commands and output: `evidence/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/production_path_audit.txt`.\n\n## 4. Eight-job / authority / denominator / repair / persistence / resume / terminal / CLI invariants (TEST item 4)\n\nDelegated to an independent, read-only agent with no access to this session's\ncontext (so it could not simply restate prior nodes' claims), instructed to\nverify each invariant from source, not from result-markdown prose. All 7\nPASS, each with file:line evidence. Full report:\n`evidence/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/invariant_audit.txt`. Summary:\n\n1. Eight model jobs, package-relative prompts/schemas, count enforced by `load_job_registry` — **PASS**\n2. Authority: routing/join/acceptance/terminal decisions read only a code-set `pending_guard`; `FORBIDDEN_MODEL_FIELDS` rejects any model schema/candidate proposing control fields — **PASS**\n3. Denominators: `compute_unit_denominator` recomputes fresh per call; `classify_join_members` rejects extra/stale/cross-unit members, fails closed — **PASS**\n4. Repair: `D20_ADMIT_UNIT_REPAIR` recomputes the diff itself, rejects stale parent hash, hard-fails on any out-of-boundary pointer — **PASS**\n5. Persistence/resume: real `SqliteSaver`; `validate_resume_inputs` refuses on any of 5 drift classes (identity/frozen_digest/executable/evidence/accepted_bytes); resume refused outside `RESUMABLE_TERMINALS` — **PASS**\n6. Terminals: exactly 6 kinds; `write_terminal` independently re-derives and downgrades unsupported claims to `SYSTEM_FAILURE`; `PAUSED_PREREQUISITE` rejected unless `pending_failure.class == \"pause\"` — **PASS**\n7. CLI: one live path (`_run_live`), fresh/resume both call `build_curriculum_factory_graph` once each; no simulation/session-bridge/Plan-25 references — **PASS**\n\n## 5. Adversarial/regression completeness, no waived tests (TEST item 5)\n\nN50's own receipt (`796e197370e4...`, PASSED, `1235 passed, 1 skipped, 406\nsubtests` at receipt time) maps every spec 17.2 adversarial row to a named\ntest (`tests/runtime/test_plan26_adversarial.py`, 26 tests, hash\n`0cbca18f412dd63b1c1a82fb535deb4ab50c8bcb8885fc02f2fa421d601c5a04`, matches\nreceipt exactly — unchanged). Per Finding F2, N90 did not stop at that\nreceipt (its ancestors were reworked afterward) and reran the complete suite\ndirectly:\n\n```\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/runtime -rs\n```\n```\nSKIPPED [1] tests/runtime/test_plan26_lock_drift.py:220: pinned generator absent (needs pip==25.3, pip-tools==7.6.0); CI installs both\n1246 passed, 1 skipped, 406 subtests passed in 145.09s (0:02:25)\n```\n\nZero failures, zero errors, zero xfail/xpass. The one skip is an\nenvironment-only gap (a pinned pip/pip-tools generator not installed on this\nhost; CI installs both per the test's own reason string) — not a test that\nwas deleted, weakened, or waived to hide a defect. This also confirms the\n`test_run_curriculum.py` / `parser_for` collection error and the\n`test_plan26_prompt_graph_controller.py` meta-harness failures N50's own\nresult markdown flagged as environment-specific (isolated-sandbox artifacts,\nnot Plan 26 runtime defects) no longer reproduce against the live repo:\n`parser_for` is confirmed absent and `build_parser` is the live API\n(`runtime/run_curriculum.py:49,121`), and the harness receipt store is\npopulated here. Full output: `evidence/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/full_suite_rerun.txt`.\n\n## 6. Activation gate (TEST items 6-7)\n\n- N50 status: **PASSED** (original receipt, and reconfirmed live in section 5).\n- N60 status: **NOT_AVAILABLE**. Its own evidence (`results/N60_LIVE_PRODUCT_PROOF.result.v1.md`) shows Codex is live-authenticated (ChatGPT subscription) and both provider hosts are network-reachable, but the Gemini CLI has no usable credential in this environment (`gemini-api-key` auth mode selected, `GEMINI_API_KEY`/`GOOGLE_API_KEY` unset, no Google account signed in) — a real, non-simulated probe failure (exit 41), reproducing the exact prerequisite spec section 20.2 lists (\"provide live credentials/network access for Codex, Gemini...\"). No partial transmission was attempted; no curriculum artifact was produced or claimed. This is an external account/credential gap, not an implementation defect — the runtime, transport, and preflight code all report ready.\n- Therefore: N60 is `NOT_AVAILABLE` solely for a recorded external prerequisite, and N50 passed (both originally and on N90's live rerun). TEST item 7's condition for `IMPLEMENTED_NOT_ACTIVATED` is met. TEST item 6's condition for `ACTIVATED` (authorized live unit + full-release proof) is not met and was not attempted, correctly.\n\n## Findings summary / rework_edges\n\n| Finding | rework_edges key | Owning node | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| F1: N40 evidence files had uncommitted post-receipt drift | `evidence_integrity_drift` | N40_CLI_CUTOVER | Resolved by N90 (`git checkout --`, restored to committed state); 0 hash mismatches remain |\n| F2: N40/N50/N60 receipts predate later N20/N30/N31/N32 rework touching graph.py/acceptance.py/repair.py | `receipt_cascade_invalidation` | harness (`prompt_graph_controller.py`), not a curriculum N-node | Closed by direct re-verification (full suite reran clean against current code); non-blocking; recommend harness auto-invalidate descendants on ancestor rework in a future hygiene pass |\n\nNeither finding recurred from a prior N90 cycle (the only prior N90 attempt\nwas interrupted before writing any finding), so neither is a second or third\noccurrence, and neither reflects ambiguous ownership or missing evidence. No\nfinding blocks this verdict.\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nAll eight invariant classes pass on direct, current-code re-verification; the\ncomplete regression/adversarial suite passes clean against the live,\nfinal (post-rework) code; the production path is singular with no forbidden\nimport or legacy fallback; every receipted artifact hash is now verified\ncurrent and valid. N60 correctly reports `NOT_AVAILABLE` for a genuine,\nevidenced external prerequisite (live Gemini credential) rather than any\nimplementation gap. Per TEST item 7, the truthful verdict is:\n\n**`IMPLEMENTED_NOT_ACTIVATED`**\n","numLines":202,"startLine":1,"totalLines":202}}}
