EDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE and D22_ACCEPT_UNIT (acceptance.py:315-382),\neach time rebuilt from current artifact_heads/deterministic_checks/\nunit_reviews state — no cached denominator is trusted. Join rejection fails\nclosed: D07_CORRELATE_AND_ADMIT_SOURCES rejects cross-unit contamination\n(sources.py:505-518), extra members (sources.py:522-525), stale\ninterpretations whose parent hash no longer matches current retrieval\n(sources.py:527-540). D12_VISUAL_BARRIER_AND_JOIN similarly rejects missing/\nextra members (visuals.py:346-354) and stale content-hash results\n(visuals.py:356-366).\n\n4. Repair invariant — PASS\nD20_ADMIT_UNIT_REPAIR (repair.py:882-989) recomputes its own diff via\njson_pointer_diff(parent_body, new_body) (line 944), never trusting a\nmodel-supplied manifest; rejects a stale parent hash at line 937-942\n(declared_parent_sha == current_hash, else SystemFailure); hard-fails any\nout-of-boundary pointer at line 946-952 (require(not out_of_bound,\n\"integrity\", ...), raising via require() -> SystemFailure, not silently\ndropped).\n\n5. Persistence/resume — PASS\nReal SqliteSaver used at persistence.py:540-545 (from\nlanggraph.checkpoint.sqlite import SqliteSaver). validate_resume_inputs()\n(persistence.py:1011-1031) enforces 5 classified drift categories across 10\nfields: identity (contract_version, run_id, created_at, engine_root,\ncurriculum_root, active_manifest_path, output_root, mode,\nrequested_unit_id), frozen_digest, executable, evidence, accepted_bytes — an\nunclassified field itself refuses resume. _validate_terminal_legality()\n(persistence.py:1034-1044) refuses resume unless the prior terminal is in\nRESUMABLE_TERMINALS = {\"INTERRUPTED\", \"PAUSED_PREREQUISITE\"}\n(persistence.py:196).\n\n6. Terminals — PASS\nExactly 6 terminal kinds (reducers.py:433-439: UNIT_ACCEPTED, COMPLETE,\nINTERRUPTED, PAUSED_PREREQUISITE, CONVERGENCE_EXHAUSTED, SYSTEM_FAILURE).\nwrite_terminal() (nodes/terminal.py:472-500) is the sole terminal-writing\nimplementa