ory -- no cwd or\nrepo-root fallback.\n\n2. Authority/routing -- PASS\n`routing.py:351-378` (`decide`) resolves destinations purely from a\n`pending_guard` record placed on state by deterministic Python nodes\n(`routing.py:327-338`, `_guard_value`), never from raw model output.\n`transport.py:58-64` defines `FORBIDDEN_MODEL_FIELDS` (accept, accepted,\nadmission, complete, decision, next_node, route, status, terminal, verdict,\netc.); `assert_no_authoritative_fields` (`transport.py:237-245`) is invoked on\nboth candidate output and the schema itself at `model_nodes.py:431,560` and\n`transport.py:725,841`, rejecting any model schema/candidate that declares a\ncontrol-plane field name.\n\n3. Denominator invariants -- PASS\n`acceptance.py:108-268` (`compute_unit_denominator`) recomputes every acceptance\ncategory (sources, domain, content, visuals, pages, review, repair) fresh from\nstate each call, filtering by `unit_id` and current head hash -- stale/cross-unit/\nduplicate records are excluded by construction, and any category miss fails the\nwhole check (`passed = all(...)`). `persistence.py:1052-1071`\n(`classify_join_members`) explicitly rejects `extra` members outside the\nexpected denominator (`raise PersistenceError(f\"completed members outside the\ndenominator: {extra}\")`) and treats a join `satisfied` only when `pending` is\nempty -- fails closed.\n\n4. Repair -- PASS\n`repair.py:882-952` (`D20_ADMIT_UNIT_REPAIR`) recomputes the parent/child diff\nitself via `json_pointer_diff` (never trusting the model's own manifest), checks\n`declared_parent_sha == current_hash` (rejects stale parents as `SystemFailure`/\n\"integrity\"), and computes `out_of_bound = [... not within_boundary(...)]`,\nraising `SystemFailure` if any changed pointer falls outside the declared repair\nboundary (`repair.py:944-952`). This is a hard `require(...)` (fail closed), not\na warning.\n\n5. Persistence/resume -- PASS\n`persistence.py:538-545` builds the real `SqliteSaver` from\n`langgraph.checkpoint.sqlite`. `validate_resume_inputs` (`persistence.py:\n1011-1031`) walks every observed field, refusing resume (`ResumeRefused`) if the\nfield is unclassified or its digest differs from the baseline, keyed by\n`_DRIFT_FIELD_CLASSES` (`persistence.py:992-1008`): identity, frozen_digest,\nexecutable, evidence, accepted_bytes. `_validate_terminal_legality`\n(`persistence.py:1034-1044`) refuses resume unless the prior terminal is in\n`RESUMABLE_TERMINALS`. `compute_resume_frontier` (`persistence.py:1074-1123`)\nrewrites any model-node destination to the classification entry rather than\nreplaying it directly, preventing replay of a committed-but-unclassified\nexternal call.\n\n6. Terminals -- PASS\n`nodes/terminal.py:48-108` defines exactly the 6 terminal kinds (UNIT_ACCEPTED,\nCOMPLETE, INTERRUPTED, PAUSED_PREREQUISITE, CONVERGENCE_EXHAUSTED,\nSYSTEM_FAILURE) in `TERMINAL_GUARDS`. `write_terminal` (`terminal.py:472-500`)\nindependently re-derives every candidate via `validate_terminal_candidate` and\ndowngrades any unsupported claim to `SYSTEM_FAILURE` (`terminal.py:446-469`),\nnever trusting the proposing guard. `_validate_paused` (`terminal.py:307-327`)\nexplicitly rejects a PAUSED_PREREQUISITE candidate if\n`pending_failure.class != \"pause\"` -- so tool/transport/schema/render/integrity/\nimplementation faults (which carry a different failure class) cannot masquerade\nas a genuine external prerequisite pause.\n\n7. CLI -- PASS\n`runtime/run_curriculum.py:527-586` (`_run_live`) is the single live path; both\nfresh (`_prepare_fresh`) and resume (`_prepare_resume`) branches call\n`build_curriculum_factory_graph` (imported at line 42) exactly once each, then\n`compiled.invoke(...)` (line 470). No references to \"simulation\",\n\"session_bridge\", or \"Plan25/plan-25\" exist anywhere in `run_curriculum.py` or\n`graph.py`. The module's own docstring (lines 1-25) explicitly disclaims holding\nany node body/guard/join/acceptance rule itself.\n\nNo FINDINGS reported by the agent -- all 7 items PASS based on direct code\ninspection, independently corroborating N20/N21/N22/N23/N30/N31/N32/N40's own\nresult claims rather than trusting them.\n","userModified":false}}
