ependently\nrecomputed by replicating the controller's own digest algorithm\n(`prompt_graph_controller.py::path_digest`/`sha256_file`) against the live\nrepository — 69 output entries across 15 receipts, **0 mismatches**. Full\nmethod and output: `evidence/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/receipt_hash_verification.txt`.\n\n| Node | Status |\n|---|---|\n| N00_BASELINE_FREEZE | PASSED |\n| N10_DEPENDENCY_API | PASSED |\n| N11_STATE_REDUCERS | PASSED |\n| N12_EVIDENCE_ARTIFACTS | PASSED |\n| N13_TRANSPORT_AUTH | PASSED |\n| N20_GRAPH_COMPILER | PASSED |\n| N21_PERSISTENCE_RESUME | PASSED |\n| N22_DETERMINISTIC_NODES | PASSED |\n| N23_MODEL_NODES | PASSED |\n| N30_UNIT_GRAPH | PASSED |\n| N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE | PASSED |\n| N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS | PASSED |\n| N40_CLI_CUTOVER | PASSED |\n| N50_ADVERSARIAL_REGRESSION | PASSED |\n| N60_LIVE_PRODUCT_PROOF | NOT_AVAILABLE |\n\n`requirements/plan26.lock` — unchanged since N10, byte-identical across every\nciting node.\n\n### Finding — N40_CLI_CUTOVER evidence non-determinism (non-blocking, per P-N90-001)\n\n**rework_edges key:** `evidence_integrity_drift` (informational only —\nexplicitly not routed as blocking rework) · **owning node:** N40_CLI_CUTOVER\n\nPer approved patch overlay P-N90-001: the baseline hash check above (0\nmismatches) was taken *before* N90 executed the full suite. Executing the\nfull suite (required by this node's own TEST/LOOP) necessarily reruns\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_cli.py::PreflightTests::test_preflight_read_only_evidence`,\nwhich writes `results/evidence/N40_CLI_CUTOVER/preflight_read_only.txt`\nembedding a fresh `tempfile.TemporaryDirectory()`-randomized path on every\ninvocation — a structural non-determinism in the test's own design that no\ncode change to N40 can fix. N90 also found a second file with the identical\nmechanism, not separately named by the patch's own enumeration:\n`test_plan25_root_refusal_evidence` similarly embeds a random tempfile path\ninto `plan25_resume_refusal.txt`. Both are the same root cause (a sibling\nevidence-writing test in the same file/suite, same randomized-tempfile-path\nshape, no other content difference); `import_audit.txt` and `cli_help.txt`\nremain byte-identical. Full diagnosis, byte-level diff evidence, and the\nreasoning for extending the patch's non-blocking treatment to the second file\nwithout treating it as a new/different kind of drift:\n`evidence/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/n40_evidence_drift_note.txt`.\n\nPer P-N90-001, this is recorded as non-blocking informational, not routed as\n`cli_or_cutover` rework: the receipted content was correct at admission time;\nonly these two already-diagnosed, non-deterministic evidence byte-streams can\nnever reproduce themselves by the tests' own design, independent of any N40\ncode defect.\n\n## 3. Exactly one compiled LangGraph production path (TEST item 3)\n\n- Single `StateGraph(...)`/`.compile(...)` pair: `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py:601,612`.\n- `run_curriculum.py` has exactly one live-execution function, `_run_live`\n  (line 527); `_run_preflight` (line 318) is explicitly read-only. Both the\n  fresh-episode branch (line 570) and resume-episode branch (line 554) call\n  the same `build_curriculum_factory_graph` exactly once each.\n- No top-level `import`/`from` of `langchain`, `openai`, or\n  `google.generativeai` anywhere under `runtime/` (`langchain_core`, LangGraph's\n  own dependency, is excluded per `implementation.graph.v3.yaml`'s\n  `forbidden_production_imports` list).\n- A legacy island — `runtime/run_state.py`, `runtime/session_bridge.py`,\n  `runtime/finalize_evidence.py`, `runtime/workbook.py` (distinct from\n  production `runtime/langgraph_factory/workbook.py`), and\n  `runtime/curriculum_factory_graph.py` (Plan 25) — is confirmed unreachable\n  from `run_curriculum.py` or any `langgraph_factory/*.py` module (direct\n  grep of both directions).\n- CLI `--help` (rerun live, current code) exposes exactly\n  `--preflight | --unit | --all | --resume`, each requiring `--authorization`\n  except read-only `--preflight` — no legacy path.\n\nFull commands and output: `evidence/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/production_path_audit.txt`.\n\n## 4. Eight-job / authority / denominator / repair / persistence / resume / terminal / CLI invariants (TEST item 4)\n\nDelegated to an independent, read-only agent with no access to this session's\ncontext, instructed to verify each invariant from source, not from result\nmarkdown prose. All 7 PASS, each with file:line evidence. Full report:\n`evidence/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/invariant_audit.txt`. Summary:\n\n1. Eight model jobs, package-relative prompts/schemas, count enforced by `load_job_registry` — **PASS**\n2. Authority: routing/join/acceptance/terminal decisions read only a code-set `pending_guard`; model-node writes are allow-listed, excluding all control/routing fields — **PASS**\n3. Denominators: `compute_unit_denominator` recomputes fresh per call; join admission rejects extra/stale/cross-unit members, fails closed — **PASS**\n4. Repair: `D20_ADMIT_UNIT_REPAIR` recomputes the diff itself, rejects stale parent hash, hard-fails on any out-of-boundary pointer — **PASS**\n5. Persistence/resume: real `SqliteSaver`; `validate_resume_inputs` refuses on any of 5 drift classes (identity/frozen_digest/executable/evidence/accepted_bytes); resume refused outside `RESUMABLE_TERMINALS` — **PASS**\n6. Terminals: exactly 6 kinds; `write_terminal` independently re-derives and downgrades unsupported claims to `SYSTEM_FAILURE`; `PAUSED_PREREQUISITE` rejected unless `pending_failure.class == \"pause\"` — **PASS**\n7. CLI: one live path (`_run_live`), fresh/resume both call `build_curriculum_factory_graph` once each; no simulation/session-bridge/Plan-25 references reachable — **PASS**\n\n## 5. Adversarial/regression completeness, no waived tests (TEST item 5)\n\nN50's own receipt is `PASSED`. N90 reran the complete suite directly against\ncurrent code:\n\n```\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/runtime -rs\n```\n```\nSKIPPED [1] tests/runtime/test_plan26_lock_drift.py:220: pinned generator absent (needs pip==25.3, pip-tools==7.6.0); CI installs both\n1246 passed, 1 skipped, 406 subtests passed in 128.14s (0:02:08)\n```\n\nZero failures, zero errors, zero xfail/xpass. The one skip is an\nenvironment-only gap (a pinned pip/pip-tools generator not installed on this\nhost; the test's own reason string states CI installs both) — not a test\ndeleted, weakened, or waived to hide a defect. Full output:\n`evidence/N90_FINAL_AUDIT/full_suite_rerun.txt`.\n\n## 6. Activation gate (TEST items 6-7)\n\n- N50 status: **PASSED** (receipt, and reconfirmed live in section 5).\n- N60 status: **NOT_AVAILABLE**. `results/N60_LIVE_PRODUCT_PROOF.result.v1.md`\n  shows Codex is live-authenticated (ChatGPT subscription) and both provider\n  hosts are network-reachable, but the Gemini CLI has no usable credential in\n  this environment (`gemini-api-key` auth mode selected, `GEMINI_API_KEY`/\n  `GOOGLE_API_KEY` unset, no Google account signed in) — a real,\n  non-simulated probe exits 41 before any curriculum content is constructed\n  or transmitted. This reproduces spec section 20.2's recorded external\n  prerequisite (\"provide live credentials/network access for Codex,\n  Gemini...\") and matches this project's standing constraint (no billed API\n  keys provisioned for this user; only Claude Code and ChatGPT Pro/Codex\n  subscriptions exist). This is an external account/credential gap, not an\n  implementation defect — the runtime, transport, and preflight code all\n  report ready (`--preflight` returns `ready: true`).\n- Therefore: N50 passed and N60 is `NOT_AVAILABLE` solely for a recorded\n  external prerequisite — TEST item 7's condition for\n  `IMPLEMENTED_NOT_ACTIVATED` is met. TEST item 6's condition for `ACTIVATED`\n  (authorized live unit + full-release proof) is not met and was not\n  attempted, correctly.\n\n## Findings summary / rework_edges\n\n| Finding | rework_edges key | Owning node | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| N40 evidence files (`preflight_read_only.txt`, `plan25_resume_refusal.txt`) embed a `tempfile`-randomized path and cannot reproduce receipted bytes on any full-suite rerun | `evidence_integrity_drift` | N40_CLI_CUTOVER | Non-blocking, informational, per approved patch P-N90-001 — structural test-design non-determinism, not an implementation defect; verified no other file/kind of drift exists |\n\nNo finding blocks this verdict. No finding recurred a second or third time\nwithin this attempt, and no finding reflects ambiguous ownership or missing\nevidence.\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nAll 7 invariant classes pass on direct, current-code re-verification; the\ncomplete regression/adversarial suite passes clean (1246 passed, 1\nenvironment-only skip, 0 failures); the production path is singular with no\nforbidden import or legacy fallback reachable; every receipted artifact hash\nis verified current and valid except a patch-covered, already-diagnosed,\nnon-blocking test-evidence non-determinism. N60 correctly reports\n`NOT_AVAILABLE` for a genuine, evidenced external prerequisite (live Gemini\ncredential) rather than any implementation gap. Per TEST item 7, the truthful\nverdict is:\n\n**`IMPLEMENTED_NOT_ACTIVATED`**\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1772,"cache_read_input_tokens":105505,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1772},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"512d45f8-5e59-47de-883c-0e101cf89d49","uuid":"6142c0c2-ebcc-4921-a34e-7bfe45cfde0f","timestamp":"2026-08-13T01:01:51.976Z","request_id":"req_011CdyqurxX6QQFc7u3eG8kH"}
